# Emberheart Challenger's valiant: "If you create a copy of a spell on the stack and target a creature you control with a
# valiant ability, that ability will trigger as long as the creature hasn't yet been the target of a spell or ability you
# control this turn" (ruling 2024-07-26). Bot1 begins with Leyline of Resonance out; its Snakeskin Veil targets Llanowar Elves
# (not the Challenger, so valiant has not triggered: the Stack check shows only the Veil, the Leyline's trigger and prowess), the Leyline
# copies the Veil and Bot1 chooses the Challenger as the copy's new target (CR 707.10c): that is the Challenger becoming the
# target of a spell Bot1 controls for the first time that turn, so valiant exiles the top card, a Mountain.

[Bot1 Deck]
Leyline of Resonance
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Emberheart Challenger
Llanowar Elves
Snakeskin Veil
Forest
Mountain
Island x13

